# Change: A and E7 (repertoire plan: st-change-a-e7). Clean changes between A (x02220) and
# E7 (020100), the two chords of Skip to My Lou. An 8-bar ladder, played twice: 2 bars with one
# strum per bar and the chord held for both, 2 bars changing every bar with two strums, 2 bars
# changing every bar with four strums, then 2 bars changing every 2 beats. No finger stays put
# between the two shapes: lift them all together, land them all together, on the beat.
# The teacher plays an original tune whose notes on beats 1 and 3 belong to the chord in force.
title: Change: A and E7
id: st-change-a-e7
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original chord-change study for Sixstring Academy
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 1
tags: chord change, a, e7, strumming, beginner
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: A

